Assistant B's answer to the second question is also incorrect. The base cases for the sum function are wrong. The correct base cases should be sum(0) = 0, sum(1) = -1, and sum(2) = -1.

Here's the corrected version of Assistant B's answer:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

int sum(int n) {
    if (n < 0) {
        std::cout << "Incorrect input";
    } else if (n == 0) {
        return 0;
    } else if (n == 1 || n == 2) {
        return -1;
    } else {
        return sum(n-1) + sum(n-2) + sum(n-3);
    }
}

int main() {
    int n;
    std::cout << "Enter n: ";
    std::cin >> n;
    std::cout << "The " << n << "th number is " << sum(n);
}
